# Analytics. Every one of these is optional: leave a variable unset and that
# tag is never loaded at all. See docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# These are inlined at build time because the site is a static export, so
# changing one requires a rebuild rather than just a redeploy.

# Google Analytics 4
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Microsoft Clarity. Recommended: enable for a week when you want session
# recordings, then remove it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=

# Meta Pixel. Only worth adding while you are actually running ads.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# Google Ads conversion tracking.
#
# Unlike the three above, these two are load-bearing: the Performance Max
# campaign bids on the conversions they report, so leaving them unset means
# paying for clicks that smart bidding cannot learn from. The deploy workflow
# fails the build if the id is missing, deliberately.
#
# The id is the account destination ("AW-..."). The label identifies the single
# "Contact" conversion action and is found under
# Goals > Conversions > Contact > Data sources > Manage.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ADS_LEAD_LABEL=

# Owner visit notification via ntfy.sh. Leave empty to disable it entirely.
#
# This is the topic the owner's phone subscribes to in the ntfy app. It is
# readable in the client bundle by anyone who looks, which is inherent to
# posting from the browser with no server to relay through. The topic is a long
# random string, so it is not guessable, only readable. Rotate it here and
# resubscribe in the app if it is ever abused.
NEXT_PUBLIC_NTFY_TOPIC=

# Online booking (Razorpay, driven by the ERP). Leave empty to disable it.
#
# Base URL of the ERP's public /web API, with no trailing slash, for example
# https://erp.example.com. The booking widget calls GET /web/config on load and
# shows the pay flow only when the ERP reports online_bookings_enabled: true.
# Unset, unreachable or switched off all render the same thing: "Online booking
# paused" with the usual WhatsApp enquiry. It is a public URL by nature (it is
# in the client bundle), and the Razorpay key id comes from the ERP at runtime,
# so there is nothing secret here. The ERP's CORS allow-list must include this
# site's origin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=
